1023: with async commits (1022) a pending swap is not replaced by the next one; the newer swap waits for the vsync tick.

Measured on the phone (10 home-screen page-swipe pairs, kern.sweet_fb counters): with backboardd's async Metal commits
about 45 % of the swaps reached the panel (~9 frames/s shown of ~19 committed); the others were replaced while their
GPU work was still running, because CoreAnimation is no longer held back by the encode. Without async commits 91 % are
shown (~15 frames/s). AppleCLCD::swap now waits (CoreAnimation's display thread, 1 ms steps) while a swap is pending,
at most until that one is 120 ms old. Only when kern.sweet_fb_gate_committed is non-zero (async commits in use).
Also: the GPU gate (0229) gave a frame 50 ms from the swap's arrival, of which the async commit had used 20 ms or more
before the frame's work was even submitted; 8 % of the frames were shown at that cap, some half drawn (wallpaper and dock,
no icons). The 50 ms now count from the submit. Applies after 1022.

